                <pb facs="0329" n="237" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg237"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hart to Mr. Hay</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogota</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-11-09"><hi rendition="#italic">November 9,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to your cable November 1, minister for foreign affairs says will pay
                    claim, but no money in the treasury; ways and means was not discussed; in a
                    cabinet meeting to-morrow minister for foreign affairs wishes to know if
                    certificates receivable for customs duties will be accepted and if you will
                    consent to take these by installments at one, two, and three months, $10,000
                    each. I have insisted upon American dollars, spot cash, but have agreed to ask
                    as above in view of the condition of the Colombian treasury. I beg to suggest
                    that I should be allowed to accept American currency by installments at one,
                    two, and three months.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hart.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
